title the dial booked before it is built
prompt Keaton granted standing permission to book new features as external research and siloed active-designing rounds when the round surfaces one.
think The QA round surfaced two real gaps rather than a list. Booked those two and nothing invented beside them.
think Gap one: Gauge names a Door/Meter dial for code comments and the dial has never been read. Keaton named code comments in the ask, so this is the reach the card is missing.
think Gap two: Service is judged, and the interesting question is which half resists counting rather than whether judgement is hard.
think Both pieces name the same falsifier -- a uniform comment-setting spread means the reading distinguishes nothing -- so the scoping note takes that measurement first and the third piece waits on the number.
obs Filed by the design-rooms test: the two arguments outlive their code and went to active-designing; the round scoping does not and went to active-development.
obs The Service essay names its own trap plainly -- a citation-graph Service rewards being pointed at rather than being useful, which is Civic Style's own finding in a new domain. The answer is to print the counted half as inputs until a graph walk agrees with twenty hand readings.
obs Recalled a stamp again inside twenty minutes -- the card cited 165120 for a file written at 165106. REDS %202's class, caught this time by tracked_link before it shipped, since a file link is a medium a guard already reaches. The habit is real, and capturing filenames into variables rather than typing them is the working fix.
obs The card went 25,100 over its 24,576 bound as the bookings landed. Condensed the Now block, whose index-fold narrative was two rounds old and lives in its own logs, and the card reads 24,496.
